"The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order (https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.6549)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.0 years ago; Title: The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order ... In 2012 Jan Saxl conjectured that all irreducible representations of the symmetric group occur in the decomposition of the tensor square of the irreducible representation corresponding to the staircase partition.\nTitle: The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order\nAuthors: Christian Ikenmeyer\nDate: Fri Oct 24 02:51:48 2014\n\nIn 2012 Jan Saxl conjectured that all irreducible representations of the symmetric group occur in the decomposition of the tensor square of the irreducible representation corresponding to the staircase partition. We make progress on this conjecture by proving the occurrence of all those irreducibles which correspond to partitions that are comparable to the staircase partition in the dominance order. Moreover, we use our result to show the occurrence of all irreducibles corresponding to hook partitions. This generalizes results by Pak, Panova, and Vallejo from 2013.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/1410.6549v2)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.0 years ago; Crawled: today; ## The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order ... In 2012 Jan Saxl conjectured that all irreducible representations of the symmetric group occur in the decomposition of the tensor square of the irreducible representation corresponding to the staircase partition.\n\n## The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order\n\nChristian Ikenmeyer\n\nPublished: 2014-10-24 | Updated: 2015-05-05\n\nComments: 11 pages\n\nNote:\n\nDOI: 10.1016/j.disc.2015.04.027\n\ngroup irreducible representation staircase symmetric group partition representation\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nIn 2012 Jan Saxl conjectured